\":49924,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.7548687,\"contextWindow\":1000000,\"maxOutputTokens\":64000,\"canonicalModel\":\"claude-sonnet-5\",\"provider\":\"firstParty\"}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"fast_mode_disabled_reason\":\"sdk_opt_in_required\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"api_error_status\":null,\"result\":\"All tests pass and only `export.go` was modified.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nFound the bug in `checkpointBranchDestinations.BranchesFor` in `internal/cli/export.go`. It checked the session's stale metadata branch (`metadataBranch`) *before* checking whether the checkpoint is reachable from the default branch (`DefaultCheckpointIDs`), so a transcript whose checkpoint originated on a now-merged feature branch kept being filed under that old branch folder instead of the default branch.\\n\\nBrain history (a prior session transcript that implemented this exact reachability check) confirmed the intended order: default-branch reachability should take priority, with the original branch preserved only as `source_branch` metadata, falling back to the metadata branch only for unmerged/unreachable checkpoints.\\n\\nFix: reordered the checks so default-branch reachability is evaluated first, falling back to the metadata branch only when the checkpoint isn't reachable from the default branch.\\n\\n```go\\nfunc (d checkpointBranchDestinations) BranchesFor(checkpointID, metadataBranch string) []string {\\n\\tif d.DefaultBranch != \\\"\\\" && len(d.DefaultCheckpointIDs) > 0 {\\n\\t\\tif _, ok := d.DefaultCheckpointIDs[checkpointID]; ok {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn []string{d.DefaultBranch}\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tbranch := strings.TrimSpace(metadataBranch)\\n\\tif branch != \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\treturn []string{branch}\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn []string{\\\"\\\"}\\n}\\n```\\n\\n`SourceBranch` was already correctly preserved in `addSelectedSession`/`addSnapshotSession`, so no other changes were needed.\\n\\nValidation:\\n- `go build ./...` \u2014 passed\\n- `go test ./internal/cli/...` \u2014 passed (full package, 93.9s)\\n\\nNo changes to `go.mod`/`go.sum`; no tests were modified.\",\"ttft_ms\":1401,\"ttft_stream_ms\":795,\"time_to_request_ms\":15,\"type\":\"result\",\"duration_ms\":202595,\"uuid\":\"3bb78cbd-2b13-44a7-98d3-d2f05c12c1a8\"}\n",
